<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Willehad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 745–789</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Saint Willehad</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Willehad (c. 745–789) was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-saxons">Anglo-Saxon</a> missionary from Northumbria who worked among the Frisians and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxons</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> sent him to the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weser">Weser</a>, and in 787 he was consecrated as the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bremen">Bremen</a>. He built the first cathedral there shortly before his death and was venerated as a saint.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/willehad.jpg" alt="Willehad" width="320" height="497" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bischof_Willehad_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
